  "claims": [
    "With n=100 vs 15 and a 4x variance ratio and NO real difference, the Student t-test rejected 37.5% of the time against a nominal 5% \u2014 7.5 times its promise.",
    "Welch on the same data rejected 4.8%, at nominal.",
    "At equal sample sizes with the same variance ratio Student rejected 5.5%, which is why the failure goes unnoticed.",
    "Student's null p-values are not uniform when its assumptions break, so its p-value is misleading at every threshold, not just at 0.05.",
    "Welch is not universally safe: on skewed unbalanced data Welch is the test running above alpha while Student happens to be nearer nominal."
  ],
